  "body": "What if your whole family could live close, while waking up every day to sweeping water and city views?\r\n\r\nSet across two cross lease titles on approx. 923sqm (more or less) on the northern slopes of Orakei, this rare dual dwelling property captures elevated views across Hobson Bay and the Auckland skyline. From soft morning light reflecting on the water to the evening city lights shimmering in the distance, the outlook here becomes part of everyday living.\r\n\r\nThis is flexibility with a view! Two separate homes on one site open up clear pathways, depending on what matters most to you.\r\n\r\nFor extended families, it means being part of each other’s daily lives while still having your own front door. Grandparents close enough for Sunday lunch. Teenagers with space to grow. Guests staying comfortably without crowding the home.\r\n\r\nFor investors, both dwellings can be rented or operated as Airbnb, offering dual income potential. Live in one and generate income from the other, or rent both while landbanking in a tightly held Orakei location known for long term capital growth.\r\n\r\nFor developers or future planners, the opportunity is significant. Zoned Residential Mixed Housing Urban, the site presents real scope to add value, whether through a substantial renovation, redevelopment, or building a dream home designed to fully capitalise on the elevated water and city views.\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\n2/33 Ngaiwi Street:\r\nPositioned to fully embrace elevated water and city views, the main residence has been renovated inside and offers generous family living across two levels, including a living area that looks out across the bay and city skyline.\r\n• 4 bedrooms\r\n• 1 bathroom\r\n• 2 living areas (upstairs and downstairs)\r\n• Kitchen positioned at the heart of the home\r\n• Expansive entertainer’s deck with water and city views\r\n• Large flat backyard lawn\r\n• Workshop space for storage or projects\r\n• Single garage plus two carports\r\n• 4 plus off-street parks\r\nThe generous flat lawn is a rare feature in Orakei’s hillside setting, offering exceptional space for children to play and families to enjoy outdoor living. With the driveway opening onto the lawn, there is also great off-road space for kids to ride their bikes and play safely. \r\n\r\nExplore full details & photos for 2/33 Ngaiwi Street here:\r\nwww.trademe.co.nz/a/property/residential/sale/auckland/auckland-city/orakei/listing/5815772379\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\n1/33 Ngaiwi Street:\r\nThe second dwelling also enjoys beautiful city and water views from the living area, flowing directly to a private deck that captures the outlook.\r\n• 2 bedrooms\r\n• 1 bathroom with 2 separate toilets\r\n• 1 living area with city and water views\r\n• Renovated interior\r\n• Private deck\r\n• Low maintenance living\r\n• An off-street parking\r\nIdeal for extended family, older children, guests or rental income, it offers flexibility now and future potential to add value or redevelop.\r\n\r\nExplore full details and photos for 1/33 Ngaiwi Street here:\r\nwww.trademe.co.nz/a/property/residential/sale/auckland/auckland-city/orakei/listing/5815772355\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\nMoments from Eastern Bays beaches, Orakei Domain, Eastridge Shopping Centre and an easy commute to the CBD. Zoned for Orakei Primary School, Selwyn College and Baradene College (Catholic), with top private schools nearby.\r\n\r\nA place where the views are beautiful, the space is generous, and the possibilities are yours to shape.",
